{"event_type":"review","id":"877d0a08ad0e0099cbc66d7eb1ded0892ff4260a073e2115983b6b79354afc4b","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T19:53:58Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1aa2c2c729b687250855cd6627a81e96145be83d4fd8d182951c7748ee9ab3c9","sha256":"1aa2c2c729b687250855cd6627a81e96145be83d4fd8d182951c7748ee9ab3c9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f19bcdf5e740213a99de7070206034938e6c46afa42519d49b9055c5670d55d5","sha256":"f19bcdf5e740213a99de7070206034938e6c46afa42519d49b9055c5670d55d5"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/23d743491fa88e18ee5aba9a54aa42180ec8b4173c3f3ea0a90ac6b16d7a4a1d","sha256":"23d743491fa88e18ee5aba9a54aa42180ec8b4173c3f3ea0a90ac6b16d7a4a1d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/68dd7bcbe7b4b250aa34366fee23995dde3a4ea5de5a6f58b2b2cbf33e6ef921","sha256":"68dd7bcbe7b4b250aa34366fee23995dde3a4ea5de5a6f58b2b2cbf33e6ef921"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4da7cbf343ee0585d401396efb62454cef1993227faf7685fb2da0796d4aec37","sha256":"4da7cbf343ee0585d401396efb62454cef1993227faf7685fb2da0796d4aec37"}],"attempt_id":"76bc3a47a6fdd2442628a3bac44ceba5be0f8607c96c6860e68a54f8643ccf7e:0:1","base":"2ed1db2bea50ca196404bb9e8e629977a30ec0df","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"e1a28238df7516d21ba876ee1cbed597055e85ee","body":"**Return early after a completed lineage with no new vendor failure.**\n\nA later review invocation calls deferred preparation before dispatch. If the latest CodeRabbit cycle is newer and has no `vendorFailure`, the completed snapshot remains active and bypasses the existing cycle-id return. A dirty tree can then fail at the clean-identity guard. A clean tree can re-import and persist the completed report again.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  if (!previous && !vendor?.vendorFailure) return undefined;\n+  // No open obligation and no new genuine outage: nothing to defer.\n+  if ((!previous || previous.vendorCompleted) && !vendor?.vendorFailure) return undefined;\n```\n\n</details>","id":"90ab6c9fca10ee9c7597bfd0a22a7c4d53cbfdec8b6c8f2183face4897eea006","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/dev/internal/deferredLedger.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Return early after a completed lineage with no new vendor failure."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"7305f80232f16052b9e73fbfa5e50e393f6a0bdf","body":"**Cap the injected review budget before agent dispatch.**\n\nWhen `remainingWallMs` returns `Infinity`, `collectBoundedReviewContext` rejects it, and the guard at `src/ops/dev/review.ts:585-587` rejects any non-finite sample before `runAgentReviewer` is called. An `agent:<role>` cycle can therefore be blocked without producing agent coverage.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     const contextDeadlineAt = Date.now() + DEFAULT_REVIEWER_TIMEOUT_MS;\n-    const contextRemaining = remainingWallMs ?? (() => contextDeadlineAt - Date.now());\n+    const contextRemaining = () =>\n+      Math.min(remainingWallMs?.() ?? Infinity, contextDeadlineAt - Date.now());\n```\n\n</details>","id":"50aed4fb016a7ffca9d6b1c77464ef27517e83537098e8887a6f4e3a983f8372","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/dev/review.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Cap the injected review budget before agent dispatch."}],"head":"33edf6713c38cb4c5639a1978c3abef710326ec6","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"4567bd7e0fb9eed7887d97d5ed6dde0d8c2b551b","intervals":[[20,21],[24,25],[43,43]],"path":"src/ops/dev/index.ts"},{"blob":"e1a28238df7516d21ba876ee1cbed597055e85ee","intervals":[[1,941]],"path":"src/ops/dev/internal/deferredLedger.ts"},{"blob":"2b5c9106fca11697a4bb4bdce2335af6